mp-units 2.5.0 (https://github.com/mpusz/mp-units), header-only C++20 library of physical units, used by the
Coulomb afterburner (build/include/CoulombUnits.h). MIT license, see LICENSE.md.

Only the headers are included here, unchanged:
  core/include     <- src/core/include     of the release
  systems/include  <- src/systems/include  of the release
Source: https://github.com/mpusz/mp-units/archive/refs/tags/v2.5.0.tar.gz
        sha256 a6bd48bee699f11f0ed5b04b8c5006d15f76e6d898e058db3880554d2e47a400

Used without CMake: the Makefile adds both include directories and -DMP_UNITS_API_CONTRACTS=1 (no contract
checking, so that gsl-lite is not needed). Needs a C++20 compiler (gcc 12 or newer, clang 16 or newer except 19)
and a formatting library: std::format of the standard library (libstdc++ of gcc 13 or newer), or else {fmt},
which is detected automatically through __has_include(<fmt/format.h>); the Makefile adds external/fmt for this
(gcc 12, e.g. Debian 12 at GSI).
